    "SketchUp Style",
    "4.4",
    "Sketch style that can be applied to a drawing created with Google SketchUp, a 3D modeling program; examples include wavy pencil lines, graphite stick marks, or quick pen strokes; often used to make a CAD model look hand-drawn. Style files are created with Googles Style Builder, which is included with SketchUp Pro 6 and 7. They may be applied to multiple drawings and can be shared between SketchUp users. NOTE: SketchUp, previously owned by Google, is now owned by Trimble. Windows Trimble SketchUp. Trimble Style Builder. Mac Trimble SketchUp. Trimble Style Builder. Style file created with ArcGIS mapping software; contains symbols and map elements, including labels, arrows, legend items, borders, backgrounds, colors, and other symbols. The ESRI.style file contains a default set of map elements, symbols, and symbol properties. It can be customized or replaced using ESRIs Style Manager. Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro.",
