    ["settings_files",
    ".C3P",
    "Construct 3 Project",
    "4.2",
    "A C3P file is a project created by Scirra Construct 3, a web application used to create 2D games without any programming. It contains the settings for the project and paths to all of the assets featured in the game, which includes images, video, and sounds. C3P file open in Scirra Construct 3 C3P files can only be opened using Construct 3. To open a C3P file, follow these steps: Open Construct 3 in a web browser. Click OPEN and choose Open from file (the other two options are to open projects stored in the cloud or browser). Navigate to the location of the C3P file and select Open. To create a C3P file, follow these steps: Open Construct 3 in a web browser. Click NEW PROJECT. Choose the settings, name the file, and select Create. Web Scirra Construct 3Free.",
    "Web Scirra Construct 3.",
    "?"],
    ["settings_files",
    ".BS7",
    "Windows 7 Boot Updater Skin",
    "4.2",
    "A BS7 file is a skin created by Windows 7 Boot Updater, a third-party program used to edit the appearance of Windows 7s boot screen. It contains setting used to adjust the boot screens background, images, and animations. BS7 files may also include replacement text for the boot screens Starting Windows and © Microsoft Corporation messages. In Windows 7 Boot Updater, users can change the animation and messages that appear on Windows 7s boot screen. They can edit the messages text, position, font color, and font size. Users can then save their custom boot screen settings as a Boot Updater skin, or BS7 file. Whenever a user creates a new Boot Updater skin, Boot Updater automatically saves the users previous skin as a BS7 file. When a user creates their first custom BS7 skin, Boot Updater automatically backs up Windows 7s default boot skin. NOTE: Windows 7 Boot Updater does not work on newer versions of Windows. You can open a BS7 file in Windows 7 Boot Updater (Windows). To do so, select File → Load boot skin. You can then edit the settings your BS7 file contains, before applying them by clicking the Apply button. Windows Windows 7 Boot UpdaterFree.",
    "Windows Windows 7 Boot Updater.",
    "?"],
    ["settings_files",
    ".TSI",
    "Traktor Settings File",
    "4.2",
    "Settings file used by Traktor, a DJ program used for making music mixes; may store audio, effects, keyboard, and layout settings; also can save settings that map a DJ controller device to the software; allows settings to be remembered and the DJ controller and Traktor software to be in sync when creating mixes. To import a TSI file, navigate to the Traktor Pro preferences, select Controller Manager, and click Import. Windows Native Instruments Traktor. Mac Native Instruments Traktor.",
    "Windows Native Instruments Traktor. Mac Native Instruments Traktor.",
    "?"],
    ["settings_files",
    ".API",
    "Adobe Photoshop Inks File",
    "4.2",
    "Settings file used by Photoshop, a raster graphics editing program; stores color settings for ink colors that are used for printing images; enables users to save and load calibrated color settings, which is useful when establishing printing properties for a specific inkjet or laser printer. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adds additional features or support for other formats to Adobe Acrobat. Mac Adobe Acrobat DC. Adobe Acrobat Reader DC. Windows Adobe Acrobat DC. Adobe Acrobat Reader DCFree.",
    "Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac Adobe Acrobat DC. Adobe Acrobat Reader DC. Windows Adobe Acrobat DC. Adobe Acrobat Reader DC.",
    "?"],
